Jim,

I've just this last couple of days put Debian 2.2 (
http://www.debian.org/ports/alpha/ ) on an AlphaStation 400 4/233. I'd
suggest reading the following:
- SRM (">>>" ROM monitor) HOWTO: http://www.alphalinux.org/faq/srm.html
- Compaq's Power Tools pages: http://www.support.compaq.com/alpha-tools/
- Debian/Alpha install docs:
http://www.debian.org/releases/stable/alpha/install

I had no problems with the following approach:
- Download Jumpstart 1.4.1 ISO image from Compaq and burn a (bootable)
CD
- Using SRM, boot from that and partition the hard disk
- Make the "official" Debian 2.2_r3 Alpha Binary 1 CD
- Boot from that and do the install

Any questions, please ask.

Toby


