Jim,
    On most of the alpha's I have worked on install is pretty straight
forward. But I would also suggest using one of the iso images to a cd.
RedHat and Suse are both bootable from srm (the VMS like thing you referred
to probably) Its should say when it boots. If  you get a GUI you are
alphaBIOS.
Usually show dev should show you all your disk devices. The load the cd and
type boot dka500 (or whatever the show dev says your cdrom is).
From then on it is just like any other install for Linux. One thing to note,
a lot of the old NT alpha's (800 I believe is one) have video cards not
supported by X. These would be most of the powerstorm (except for the
permidia one, 4d10t I think). If you have one of these you can not use X.
Better to replace with matrix or something. Or use VMS or TRU64 or NT which
do support them.

Hope this helps.

Niles



