I am not sure what you mean by "RH" above but if these are supposed to
be relatively recent, like say for the last year and a half at least and
maybe longer - I have no way or time to check, Red Hat distributions
then all statements above are trivially falsified by a simple
confrontation with Reality. :-)

What is even more - for quite a while Red Had officially "does not
support" booting through milo (which does not mean that you cannot do
that but that you are on your own if you try) and a kernel included in
7.1 may be not even fit for that purpose (once again, nothing says
that you cannot use something else with 7.1 binaries).

RH installer indeed will NOT write a boot block if it will not find a
space for it outside of what is listed in your partition table.  If you
_know_ that this is ok then it is up to you to use '-f' flag on
'swriteboot'.  Installer refuses to be "smart" and IMO this is a good
thing.

