>Let's face it, somehow the original GS320 got 155K tpmC on such an
>uninteresting commercial benchmark as TPC-C while the E10k languished
>at 115K.  And somehow the GS320 is now at 231K while the E10k is at
>157K.  Let's face it, that's 50% higher even though it's using half as
>many processors.
