> Linux stores the time differently than the SRM console.  There are 3
different
> operating systems that store time, and they all do it differently.  Just
set
> the clock from Linux.

The SRM console stores the date and time into a BB_WATCH ie., one of those
battery backed up watch chips like you find in a cheap watch; the data is
typically stored as six bytes of year, month, day, hour, minute, second,
sometime as binary and sometimes as BCD.

Why some operating systems store something other than the current date and
time is a mystery.




