"Terry C. Shannon" <terryshannon@mediaone.net> wrote in message
news:Be047.9753$bj6.3386497@typhoon.ne.mediaone.net...
One question is particularly badly constructed, the one about future plans.

The choices were "migration from alpha to ia64", "stay thru ev7 then migrate
elsewhere", "stay thru ev68, then migrate elsewhere", etc.

This is too simplistic a view.  Just as the VMS VAX to Alpha experience was
different from the unix MIPS to Alpha experience, the choices that an ISV or
customer faces are more complicated.

The major strategies that I see are:
 - stay with Alpha for existing and new apps, migrating to ia64 at the
appropriate time
 - stay with Alpha for existing apps, evalutate the platform for new apps
case by case
 - stay with Alpha for existing apps, all new apps to something else
 - support Alpha and a second platform other than ia64 from compaq
 - plan to move to a non-compaq platform in an orderly fashion
 - initiate a program to eliminate the cost of supporting alpha asap

And the answer is different for VMS and unix, with many ISVs and customers
dealing with both.  Since most Tru64 customers have Solaris in their
environment today, my guess is that they will eliminate Tru64 as quickly as
possible so that they can bring in a second credible alternative to Solaris.




