WRONG !

The -a's and -au's come preloaded with both the AlphaBIOS and the SRM
console

The default for the -a is the AlphaBIOS, and the default for the -au is the
SRM.

To load the SRM console on the  -a - go to F2 setup

Scroll down to CMOS settings, then hit F6

This will show (at the bottom of the screen) the default console setting
There you can change it to SRM unix or SRM VMS - heit F10 twice and power
cycle the system

You'll also need, for Tru64 a SRM compatible SCSI controller (QLogic or NCR)
and a Tru64 graphics card
With Linux SRM you'll probably just need the SCSI ctr above
With VMS - add a SCSI CDROM and one of the 7 or 8 supported video cards

