> 1)
> Do I need SRM ? I remember someone wrote aboot was better than
> MILO, but forgot reasons. Where can I find recent Firmware?

You can get SRM images at
ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/Alpha/firmware/index.html
(for the lx board bottom left)
SRM is very powerful for doing machine settings. A little bit of learning is
indeed needed.You can get the SRM Howto at http://www.alphalinux.org/.

>
> 2)Which SCSI card do you recommend? Is the card  recognized by
> SRM and AlphaBIOS
> and, bootable from a HDD connected to it?

As far as I remember you can't boot from an Adaptec controller, so a QVision
or a NCR chip should be taken.
(I don't remember if this was only for Tru64, if anyone knows, please
respond)
I have a QVision controller.

> 3)Which type of HDD do you recommend SCSI or IDE?

Linux should work from IDE. SCSI is faster for small files. But taken into
account the cost for hostadapter and that a SCSI HD costs 2-3 times more
than it's IDE equivalent (in size) the choice is up to you. AFAIR Tru64 only
boots from SCSI HDs.

> 4) If I install an IDE HDD something like 60GB, is the HDD recognized by
> SRM and AlphaBIOS, and bootable?

should be. but be sure to have the latest versions of the firmware

