> sends shudders down my spine knowing that what "Joe" just wrote, "Suzie" can
> overwrite in a blink, and with out file version numbering, there is no way
> that the original data can be save/recovered.

It sounds like a good place for Plan 9. I always admired the way it does
HSM and resource sharing.

Sun had "the network is the computer." Plan 9 was "what network?"
Resources get shared and it begins to make less difference whether
they're local or a machine down the hall. The network is transparent,
where other OSes never let you forget that there's a network.

I'm hoping that some of the optical technologies will allow sharing of
resources at a lower level so that the system bus can be spread across
the network, for instance. As bus speeds climb, I would think that
optical will become attractive. Need another CPU for a day? Just assign
it to this machine.

The "bandwidth" of optical is large enough, but I'm not sure about
latency. 

