There's nothing inherent in your diagram above (with the 'fileserver'
entries removed) that would prevent the client/storage box interface from
being an internal one in a single box supporting both - which also halves
the total number of links required.  But the clients have to trust each
other a lot more than when they're separated from the storage servers and
can rely upon storage-server protection mechanisms.  Clients that cooperate
to export a single, stable application to a much wider external world (e.g.,
