You mean the system comes up with 640x480 standard resolution? Watch 
the boot messages. If it says something like "vga0" and "standard VGA" 
while booting, you simply do not have the correct graphics driver. 
Visit the Compaq homepage, click your way through to "Open3D" and 
select your device. You'll need to know the correct "Compaq" name for 
it, something like "Powerstorm XXX". Hopefully you can dig this out.

Open3D is a setld package; you just need to load it wiht setld -l, then 
build a new kernel (I think setld does it automatically), and reboot, 
and you should be fine.

