> Now, there are two separate meanings for clustering. There's the
> load-balancing type clustering, where multiple nodes run the same
> applications and share tasks with each other simultaneously to work on
> bigger workloads. Then there is the failover type clustering, where it
> simply a high-availability option. Which one is cited here?
