I heard reports (second hand and not sure how reliable) that a kernel
used by an installer in 7.1 distribution is compiled without
CONFIG_ALPHA_LEGACY_START_ADDRESS (a configuration parameter from 2.4
kernels).  This is _required_ by some "high end" Alphas but will kill
booting from milo.  If this is really the case then use floppies made
from 7.0 images for an installation.  This should work.  After an
installation you can always boot from a floppy for the first time and
reconfigure and recompile any kernel you want.  You are not tied to the
one which comes with a given distribution.  If you boot over a network
you likely have SRM anyway. :-)

