Trouble is, at least some of those other cluster facilities (SUN's and
Tru64, for two) *do* have file systems that

a) allow concurrent access to the same data from multiple nodes and

b) include robust access and distributed (byte-range) lock management
facilities for that data that survive the loss of any node without requiring
client applications to do anything but wait for storage fail-over and lock
state re-build to occur (though it's reportedly not as fast as in a VMS
environment - something on the order of a minute, unless they've improved
the speed lately).

In other words, rather a lot like the distributed facilities RMS provides on
VMS.  Tru64 even supports decent distributed caching as of its new release,
IIRC (whatever SUN supports in this area would likely be whatever NFS
supports).

I've told comp.os.vms this multiple times over the past year or two, but
your hearing seems to be permanently impaired.

